    "topic": "Christmas crackers were invented to sell sweets",
    "summary": "Tradition says London confectioner Tom Smith invented crackers in 1847 as a development of his bon-bon sweets, sold in a twist of paper. As bon-bon sales slumped he looked for promotional ideas; he was inspired to add a 'crackle' after hearing a log crackle on his fire. The product was first marketed as the Cosaque (French for Cossack). The sweet was eventually dropped for a trinket, and his son Walter Smith introduced the gifts, paper hats and varied designs.",
